  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When Servette FC faced financial collapse, businessman Paul-Annik Weiller supplied the money that kept the Geneva club operating. As president from 1992 to 1996, he made youth development a priority, regularly attending junior matches and wanting locally trained players to progress through the club. On leaving the presidency, he cleared more than fourteen million Swiss francs of debt.\n\nHe also succeeded his father as president of Les Amis de l'Œuvre Wallerstein, the charitable association responsible for the hospital at Arès. The association had been established to provide medical care for people without means and owned the hospital and its grounds.",
